1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:02,433
A spacecraft can fly past
a planet,

2
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:05,567
fire no engines, and leave
faster than it arrived.

3
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:09,233
Watch from the planet first.
Gravity pulls it in,

4
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:11,233
swings it around, and lets
it go.

5
00:00:11,933 --> 00:00:15,133
Measured from the planet, it
leaves about as fast as it

6
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:17,500
arrived. Only its direction
has changed.

7
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:20,533
But the planet is moving
around the Sun.

8
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:23,533
Seen from the Sun, that
curve is carried along with

9
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:25,667
it, and the spacecraft
leaves faster.

10
00:00:26,367 --> 00:00:29,700
The energy isn't free. It's
borrowed from the planet's

11
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:32,500
own orbit, by an almost
imperceptible amount.

12
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:36,333
Same flyby. Two answers.
Both of them right.
